{
  "dom_id": "question-95131",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "The systolic blood pressure of a group of people is normally distributed with a mean of $\\mu \\,\\text{mm}\\,\\text{Hg}$ and a standard deviation of $14\\,\\text{mm}\\,\\text{Hg}.$ Additionally, $60%$ of the people have a systolic blood pressure between $0.9\\mu \\,\\text{mm}\\,\\text{Hg}$ and $1.1\\mu \\,\\text{mm}\\,\\text{Hg}.$ Find the percentage of people with a systolic blood pressure lower than $110\\,\\text{mm}\\,\\text{Hg}.$\n\n*Hint: A table of values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p$ is given below, where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.75\\,$ | $\\,0.80\\,$ | $\\,0.85\\,$ | $\\,0.90\\,$ | $\\,0.95\\,$ | $\\,0.97\\,$ | $\\,0.99\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,0.6745\\,$ | $\\,0.8416\\,$ | $\\,1.0364\\,$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.8808\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n*In addition, you're given the following table of values for $p=Φ(z)$*.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.2578\\,$ | $\\,0.2546\\,$ | $\\,0.2514\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.2912\\,$ | $\\,0.2877\\,$ | $\\,0.2843\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.3264\\,$ | $\\,0.3228\\,$ | $\\,0.3192\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "",
